THOUGHT: NullAway complains because in the copy constructor, if `original` is null we return early without initializing the non-null fields `transparentcolor` and `absolutePath`. To fix this, we can delegate to the no-arg constructor (which initializes both fields) using `this();` at the start of the copy constructor, and remove the early return. Then we must run the build to confirm the NullAway error count decreases by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '46,51c\  public MapImage(MapImage original) {
    this();
    super(original);

    if (original == null) {
      return;
    }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/tilemap/xml/MapImage.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "MapImage" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

